## The re-check: two arms on the same build

**The two arms:**
- **On** = p4s7's items: setup, critic, code, fixes, read, claims (`LDR_DEEP_FIX=all,read,claims`). Budget 171 / 47
  min whole-run (Fix 6).
- **Off** = the deep profile with no items. Budget 120 / 30 min of research, then the report. This is the matched
  research time of every stage 3.
- Both arms:
  - report effort medium, citation check xhigh;
  - `LDR_MODEL_PROFILE=qwen4-flash LDR_ALLOW_DRAFT_PROFILE=1`;
  - SearXNG only, no paid search.

**How it runs:**
- Plan `queue-plan-q4d1.json`, labels q4on / q4off.
- Run `run-ldr.sh stop` first, because the queue does not restart LDR for a profile change.
- Both arms of a question run back to back, alternating which goes first (ABBA), so web drift hits both.

| order | questions | why | GPU h |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | o02 | Add-ons won most on Flash-Next (5.0 -> 10.0 of 12, p4base vs p4s6, one round). Tests setup + item 5 (dated prices). | ~5.7 |
| 2 | o01 | Setup, code tool, version check (6.0 -> 8.5 of 10). | ~5.7 |
| 3 | If Phase 5 has started: the four harder ones (p5c1b, p5c2, p5c5, p5c6). If not: h02 + h05 as regression canaries only. | Screen and hard checkables do not separate setups (pristine LDR got 15/15 and 10/10; every arm got 5/5). Until Phase 5, the harder four stay unseen. | ~4.8 / ~2.4 |
| 4 | o03, only if Karl's first look is >= 6 h away | The control: add-ons did not help here on Flash-Next (11.5 -> 10.5). | ~5.7 |

**Totals:** core ~16 GPU h (~18.4 h if Phase 5 has started), with step 0 included. ~22-24 h with o03. Time held for
chats and Jan jobs comes on top. Each pair is graded when it ends, so Karl's first look sees every finished pair.

**Time limits:**
- Each run has bench2's hard stop: on 291 / 137 min, off 240 / 120 min (open / checkable).
- An on-arm run longer than its budget + 10 % is noted. Fix 6 still uses Flash-Next's seconds (deep/checks.py EST).

**Rules, both arms:**
- bench.lock, with children started `8>&- 9>&-`.
- Nothing CPU-heavy while a run is timed.
- MemAvailable floor 12 GB, never lowered. If Qwen4 cannot keep it, stop and tell Karl.
- Kernel-log check after every run. Page-allocation failure only: drop the run and go on. Anything else: stop.
- Swap rule: engine VmSwap > 0, or a >= 4 MB swap streak, fails the run.

## Grading

- **Open questions:**
  - `blind-open.py`, BLIND_OUT=`blind-q4d1`, BLIND_DROP="Setup check,Check these,Version check,Arithmetic
    check,Consistency check", inline marks stripped.
  - **One fresh grader per question, both arms in ONE round**, against my-research/ with the real hardware. The grader
    brief carries the run date.
  - Grades go to grades.jsonl before the key is opened: points and wrong claims per report.
- **Optional anchor, no GPU:** Flash-Next's saved p4s7 report as a third blind report in the same round, on o01 and o03
  only (o02's prices are dated). This is the only fair Qwen4 vs Flash-Next view; grades from earlier rounds are not
  compared.
- **The harder four:** the Answer-section rule, blind (correct / wrong commitment / hedged / non-answer). Canaries:
  `bench2.py grade` plus wall time.
- **After the grades:** check the check sections' flags by hand (right or false).

## Decision

- **Keep the add-ons** (on becomes Qwen4's default for the next stage) when all of these hold:
  - the smoke is clean;
  - on >= off on the open total, and no question is lower by more than 1 point;
  - wrong claims are not higher by more than 2 in total;
  - no checkable flips from correct to not correct;
  - every on-arm run ends within budget + 10 %.
- **Re-tune first** (no more arms until it is fixed) on any of these:
  - an add-on fails on Qwen4: fix it and run the smoke again;
  - on is lower on the open total, or lower by >= 2 on one question;
  - Fix 6 runs over or cuts checks: re-measure EST on Qwen4;
  - repeated context-400s, compaction loops or ladder drops: re-check the profile's sizes and efforts.
- **Anything in between:** stop and ask Karl.

## Not on day one

- Porting our Strata series to Qwen4, or its exactness / KL / distribution gates. Day one uses the stock build only.
- The code-tool question (240 min, ~10 GPU h a pair).
- The holdout (Phase 5's 25 + o04-o06).
- Re-tuning sizes (C3c), efforts, workers or Fix 6's EST.
- Quant comparisons.
- Item 7 paid search, item 8, API arms.
- Moving Jan's runner, the on-demand launcher or 8080's default to Qwen4.
- Marking the profile `measured`.
- Anything on GitHub without Karl's typed OK.

